    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `membershipTier` field is derived in `OwnerMapper` at DTO-mapping time (on `GET /api/owners/{id}`), but the GOLD rule depends on a household-member count that must be snapshotted **at create time** (\"after this create\") \u2014 the mapper has no access to the service layer, so I persisted the count.\n\n1. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Schema** \u2014 added a `household_size` column to the `owners` table in all four dialect schemas (`hsqldb` \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after household resolution (`joinHousehold`), it now sets `owner.setHouseholdSize(householdSize(owner))`. The new `householdSize` helper counts existing owners sharing the resolved `householdId` and adds 1 for the owner being created (a household of one when there's no `householdId`).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` expression now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\nIn the test's scenario: owner 1 (no household yet) \u2192 size 1; owner 2 joins \u2192 both get a `householdId`, owner 2 size 2; owner 3 joins \u2192 two existing members + itself = size 3 \u2192 `GOLD`. \u2705",
